    "\n",
    "The idea is to use the cost-complexity measure to replace Gini impurity to grow the tree. The cost-complexity measure is gotten by adding the total number of end nodes with the coefficent `ccp_alpha` to the Gini impurity. The parameter `ccp_alpha>=0` is known as the **complexity parameter**, and it can help the tree to self-balance the number of end nodes and the Gini impurity.\n",
